WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.410
MICHAEL ANTON: Good evening.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:08.540
My name is Michael Anton.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.520
I am a lecturer
and research fellow

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:14.360
here at the Kirby Center, which
means that I have teaching

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:15.540
duties, among other things.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.810
I taught a class Monday, I
taught a class last night.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.460
Some of my students
are even here tonight,

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:21.085
and they shall withhold
further comment

00:00:21.085 --> 00:00:26.540
until evening is over as to
the quality of instruction.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:28.040
We have students.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:30.170
Many of you are familiar
with the college's program

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:30.870
in Washington.

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.990
But for those of you who
aren't, just reiterate,

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:35.360
say, four year liberal
arts college in Michigan.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:39.170
But every semester, a small
number, usually around 20,

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:41.780
take a semester and
come here as part

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:44.000
of their college experience.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.010
They work an internship
somewhere in Washington.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:48.302
That could be on the Hill,
it could be in a think tank,

00:00:48.302 --> 00:00:50.993
could be in an executive
branch agency, a nonprofit.

00:00:50.993 --> 00:00:52.910
And then they take all
their classes at night.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:55.220
So imagine, have
a little sympathy,

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:57.230
if you work 9:00 to
5:00 and then you

00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:00.470
got to drag yourself in here and
listen to me for three hours,

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.660
starting at 6 o'clock,
it's hard on them.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:04.670
But they do very good
work, they work hard.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:06.830
And they're an impressive
bunch, and you'll

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.720
be able to meet some
of them tonight.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:14.240
And in fact, one of them will
be introducing our speaker.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.770
I was sort of asked
to say something

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:17.145
about the topic
of our speaker, I

00:01:17.145 --> 00:01:19.640
think because I served on
the National Security Council

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:20.180
for a time.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.010
And it's presumed that I
know something about this.

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:24.710
Unfortunately, I don't really.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:27.540
But I do have one
very small story.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:30.230
I was a speechwriter for a
time on the National Security

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:32.820
Council back in the
Bush administration.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:35.780
And I was the foreign policy
speechwriter for the president.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:42.200
And the president, he had a sort
of a policy Interagency Working

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:45.290
Group that was to determine the
new space policy for the United

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:46.160
States.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:49.255
And it went on for
many, many months.

00:01:49.255 --> 00:01:51.380
And toward the end they
said, well, the president's

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:53.270
going to roll out
the space speech.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:55.563
And I got assigned
the space speech,

00:01:55.563 --> 00:01:57.980
so I got to go to the final I
don't know, five or so weeks

00:01:57.980 --> 00:01:59.400
of meetings to figure this out.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.280
And I remember asking,
when I was assigned

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:04.482
the speech, my boss,
I said, I'm supposed

00:02:04.482 --> 00:02:05.690
to be the foreign policy guy.

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:07.680
But lately, you've been
giving me immigration,

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.470
you've been given me the
Patriot Act speeches,

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:10.699
you've just been
sort of piling it on.

00:02:10.699 --> 00:02:12.357
And this is getting
a bit difficult.

00:02:12.357 --> 00:02:14.440
What does this have to do
with my official duties?

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:18.910
And my boss said, well,
you know, space is foreign.

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:19.940
[LAUGHTER]

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:22.735
So I wrote the space speech.

00:02:22.735 --> 00:02:24.110
Now, my mother
loved that speech.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.070
She was very impressed by it.

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:27.070
She watched it on television
and called me later

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:28.280
to tell me how great it was.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.852
It was not a hit at the time.

00:02:29.852 --> 00:02:32.060
This would have been, I
think around January of 2004.

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:33.660
And it was widely ridiculed.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:35.510
This was when President Bush
announced that we would go back

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:37.470
to the Moon, we would
eventually move onto Mars,

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:38.040
and things like that.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.040
And people thought it was
an election year ploy.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:44.660
And it wasn't a hit, and it was
famously the subject of comedy

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:48.470
skit on a show I can't quote
because this is a family

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:49.460
college.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:52.160
But it's on YouTube, and
it was widely ridiculed.

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:54.410
And I think that's the way
it's most remembered today.

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:55.710
But fast forward a little bit.

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:58.610
So I was working in
a job in Manhattan,

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:00.563
and I got invited
at the last minute

00:03:00.563 --> 00:03:01.730
to go out to a small dinner.

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:03.560
And I show up, and it's
one friend of mine,

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:06.185
a bunch people I don't know, and
one person whom I didn't know,

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:07.190
but I recognized.

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:10.610
And it was Neil deGrasse
Tyson, of all people.

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:13.610
The famous TV astronomer
and astrophysicist.

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:15.513
I don't know how it came up.

00:03:15.513 --> 00:03:16.680
I don't think I volunteered.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.020
He somehow dragged
out of me that yeah, I

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:19.100
wrote the space speech.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.690
And I thought, here
it comes, right?

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:22.630
He's just going to beat
the heck out of me.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:23.580
But actually he was
very nice about it.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:25.820
He said that he had
consulted on the policy

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:29.060
and he thought the policy was
actually pretty sound with one

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:30.497
or two reservations.

00:03:30.497 --> 00:03:32.330
And he remembered the
speech, and he gave me

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:33.380
a critique of it right there.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:35.480
He said, these are the three
things you really screwed up.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.397
But as for the rest of
it, it was pretty good.

00:03:37.397 --> 00:03:40.070
And I thought, well,
it could be worse.

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:43.010
All right, now, the actual
introduction of our speaker

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:45.050
will come from, as
I said, a student.

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:48.170
One of the, we call him
the WHIP students, which

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:51.470
stands for Washington
Hillsdale Internship Program,

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:53.600
her name is Riley Arlihouse.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.700
She is a junior at the
college where she's

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:57.590
studying politics and Spanish.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:00.470
She's originally from
Missouri City, Texas.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:03.710
And I'll have you know, she's
also the daughter of an Air

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:05.240
Force officer herself.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:07.430
She's currently interning
at the Heritage Foundation

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:09.330
during her semester here.

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:12.290
Please welcome me in joining
Riley to introduce our speaker.

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:16.050
[APPLAUSE]

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:20.510
RILEY ARLIHOUSE: Good evening.

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:21.880
Thank you for coming.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:24.910
Our speaker tonight
is Steven L. Kwast.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:27.700
Steve Kwast is a retired
Air Force general

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.730
and former commander of the Air
Education and Training Command

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:33.530
at Joint Base San
Antonio Randolph.

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:35.530
A graduate of the
United States Air Force

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:38.290
Academy with a degree in
astronomical engineering,

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:40.990
he holds a master's
degree in public policy

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:43.780
from Harvard's Kennedy
School of Government.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:47.200
He is a past president of the
Air Force's Air University

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.600
in Montgomery, Alabama,
and a former fighter

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:53.800
pilot with extensive combat
and command experience.

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:57.820
He is the author of the study
"Fast Space Leveraging Ultra

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:02.260
Low Cost Space Access for
21st Century Challenges."

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:05.320
And tonight he will be speaking
on the urgent need for a US

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:06.580
space force.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:08.890
Please join me in
welcoming Steve Quast.

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:13.111
[APPLAUSE]

00:05:15.456 --> 00:05:18.390
STEVEN QUAST: So Riley is
an example of our future.

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:21.690
And that's really what we're
going to be talking about.

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:23.100
But history does repeat itself.

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.545
So Michael, I have your speech.

00:05:24.545 --> 00:05:26.420
And that's the one I'm
going to give tonight.

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:29.130
So you should probably
recognize it a bit.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:30.210
But Riley, thank you.

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:32.170
And you truly are the future.

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:36.480
And that's why this is
such a happy conversation.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.100
But it's also one
reason why it's

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.440
such an important conversation.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:44.670
Because life has always been
a competition, ultimately

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:47.200
a competition of values.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:50.180
And everything else is
wrapped around that.

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:53.240
But when we asked
this question about,

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:55.250
do we need a space force?

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:56.930
I'd like to unpack
that a little bit,

00:05:56.930 --> 00:06:00.290
because it's important
to first start with why.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:02.270
Why do we need a space force?

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:04.970
And once we understand
why we need a space force,

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:07.460
then we can talk about,
well, when do we need it,

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:09.920
and what should it do?

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:11.990
Critical elements of
this central question

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:13.490
we're going to
explore this evening,

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:16.200
and I'm looking forward
to your questions.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:19.580
But one of the most
important points of thinking

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:23.420
is first understanding
what's going on around you.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:24.440
What's happening?

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.160
What is the context here?

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.780
Why is this important?

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:30.920
And as a historian,
reflecting on the fact

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:32.990
that, throughout the
history of mankind,

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:36.860
at least everything we
can read and understand,

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:40.440
technology has always
changed world power.

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:42.680
Whether it was the
caveman that figured out

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:48.320
how to harness the power of fire
to keep his or her tribe warm

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:51.380
and survive the cold winters
and cook the food so they didn't

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:53.900
die from bacteria
and other things,

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:58.940
they had a competitive advantage
and their DNA survived.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:01.770
Their values survived.

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:04.410
To the invention of the
airplane, the nuclear weapon,

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:06.890
you take a look at
any technology that

00:07:06.890 --> 00:07:12.440
has been optimized by a
certain tribe, civilization,

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:18.410
it can become a tool of national
power that changes world power.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:23.210
Space is going to change world
power because of the power

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:24.690
of space and what it can do.

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:27.740
And we're going to explore
that a little bit tonight.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:31.460
But it's also a story of
human nature and culture.

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:36.320
As a missionary kid growing
up in a tribal African area,

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:39.970
I can tell you that
world paradigms clash,

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:45.980
and they can trap a civilization
into a certain world paradigm.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:49.030
And this human
nature will not only

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:50.560
embrace something
that helps them,

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:54.190
but it also will
reject anything new.

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:57.160
And this idea of a
space force is very new,

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:59.260
and is experiencing the same.

00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:02.260
But this is not new in time.

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:05.740
A small island
nation like England

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:09.340
could dominate the world economy
and become the most powerful

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:11.800
military, economic,
and political force

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.560
on planet Earth as a
small island nation,

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:17.440
because they optimized the
development of deep sea

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:19.750
navigation and sail
and ships and the Navy.

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:26.640
But the story of rejecting
new and holding and clinging

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:30.780
to the paradigms of the past
is why no civilization has ever

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:33.030
lasted forever.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:36.120
And values are trumped
by other values

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:38.130
when another
civilization figures out

00:08:38.130 --> 00:08:40.610
a way of finding a
competitive advantage.

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:43.590
And in England, probably
the most famous story

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:47.460
is World War I. In
1914, the English

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:50.520
were hungry to go to war with
Germany, because they were

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:55.380
certain that their
superior tactics,

00:08:55.380 --> 00:09:00.120
and the Napoleonic method of
warfare that they had refined

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:03.840
to a perfect art, that
had dominated the globe,

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:06.160
would dominate once again.

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:09.660
And even though there were
historians and technologists

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:12.590
and strategists that
pointed out the machine

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:17.970
gun and the development
of poison gas,

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:20.610
the leadership said, we
don't have time for that.

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:23.640
The courage, the nobility,
and the aggressiveness

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:25.740
of our fighters were overcome.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:29.760
Our single rifles will just
overwhelm that machine gun

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:30.870
nest.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:34.290
And we'll just hold our
breath and run through the gas

00:09:34.290 --> 00:09:35.860
and fight on the other side.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:44.780
And after England lost an
entire generation of Englishmen,

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:47.630
they turned to their most
respected intellect, Dr.

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:49.670
Fisher, and asked
the question, why did

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:52.653
we lose an entire generation?

00:09:52.653 --> 00:09:54.320
And he said, you
didn't lose because you

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:56.660
had inferior technology.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:10:00.697
You had the best
technology on planet Earth.

00:10:00.697 --> 00:10:02.780
It wasn't your tactics,
your tactics were perfect.

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:08.180
You lost an entire
generation because of a lack

00:10:08.180 --> 00:10:11.880
of vision and strategy.

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:14.370
Sun Tzu in The Art of
War talks about this.

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:18.125
It's not about the technology,
it's about the strategy.

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:22.980
And so here we sit today.

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:24.930
Back in that day,
those historians

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:29.100
and the technologists brought
to the leadership of England

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:32.240
this counsel that they needed
to invest in the machine

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:34.890
gun and gas, or
at least find ways

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:37.350
of fighting through those,
because those would change

00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:39.750
the character of war.

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:42.130
And they ignored it,
saying we've got time.

00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:44.940
We've been the best, so we
will be the best, projecting

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:46.050
the past into the future.

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:52.680
We do the same today.

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:56.490
And this community
in America brought

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:58.930
the technologies
that are emerging,

00:10:58.930 --> 00:11:01.260
and the strategies that are
emerging internationally

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:03.750
and domestically to
this administration.

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:09.470
And this administration
said, build a space force.

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:13.520
But the reason space
is so powerful is not

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:19.550
that it just has a military
application like a machine gun.

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:23.810
It's because it will transform
the four major engines

00:11:23.810 --> 00:11:28.100
of economic growth that
have been consistent

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:29.840
throughout mankind.

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:36.440
Transportation, information,
manufacturing, and probably

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:41.390
most important, the ability
to deliver that transportation

00:11:41.390 --> 00:11:44.990
and information with energy.

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:48.170
Energy, the seed corn
of all development,

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:51.840
all growth, all
survival, energy.

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:54.020
So energy, transportation,
information,

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:55.550
and manufacturing--

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:57.710
these are the things
that change humanity,

00:11:57.710 --> 00:11:59.630
that will change world power.

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:03.740
And they are descending upon us
in ways that are very unique.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:06.740
The technology is on the
engineering benches today.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:08.690
But most Americans
and most in Congress

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:13.700
have not had time to really look
deeply at what's going on here.

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:17.870
But I've had the benefit of 33
years of studying and becoming

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:22.620
friends with these engineers
and these scientists.

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:26.460
This technology
can be built today

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:29.760
with technology that is not
developmental to deliver

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:31.800
any human being from any
place on planet Earth

00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:34.230
to any other place
in less than an hour,

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:36.990
to deliver Wi-Fi from
space, where you never

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:39.360
need a cell tower to connect.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.490
To deliver energy from
space where you never

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:44.520
have to plug your phone
in and it trickle charges,

00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:47.980
and you can use that
energy over time.

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:52.350
It can be applied
to cars, to houses.

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:54.660
The technology of
Edison and Tesla

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:57.270
that we live with in our energy
environment, our paradigm

00:12:57.270 --> 00:13:01.420
today, is expensive, it's
dangerous, and it's wasteful.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:02.700
Plug it into the wall.

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:04.710
But yep, that's what
we all do, because we

00:13:04.710 --> 00:13:07.950
are used to paradigms.

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:11.220
The power of space will
change world power forever.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:13.440
And it doesn't have to be
a big country to do it.

00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:15.760
It can be a small island
country, let's say,

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:18.240
New Zealand.

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:21.630
Because the technology,
if optimized,

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:23.280
can change world power.

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:26.160
And there's nothing you can do
if you don't have that power.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:28.770
The nature of power,
you either have it

00:13:28.770 --> 00:13:31.920
and your values rule,
or you do not have it

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:33.990
and you must submit.

00:13:33.990 --> 00:13:37.010
We see that play out again
and again in history,

00:13:37.010 --> 00:13:39.000
and it's playing out now.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.920
But we get trapped.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:45.990
Here in America, for example,
three times in the last hundred

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:48.480
years, we have
failed to optimize

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:53.760
the technologies that were
coming about, to our own peril.

00:13:53.760 --> 00:13:57.510
In 1920, the country
turned to General Pershing

00:13:57.510 --> 00:13:58.950
and General MacArthur.

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:02.550
That's the Father MacArthur, the
two Medal of Honor recipients,

00:14:02.550 --> 00:14:04.200
father and son.

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:06.760
In 1920, they asked
them the question,

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:10.080
should the aeroplane be
developed independently?

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:11.820
Should the tank
and mechanization

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:14.070
be developed independently?

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:15.720
And they said, absolutely not.

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:18.780
And they dictated that
the airplane and the tank

00:14:18.780 --> 00:14:20.910
must be developed
by the infantry,

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:23.400
because the infantry
is the main event.

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:26.640
The Signal Corps
is the main event.

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:30.360
And that fatal decision by the
most respected and heralded

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:36.510
heroes of the age cost thousands
of lives in World War II,

00:14:36.510 --> 00:14:40.020
because the development of
the airplane and the tank

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:42.480
were insufficient
for the competition.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:45.030
And at that time,
it was Germany.

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:48.300
We lost more airmen in the
European theater than all

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:51.180
of the Marines in World War II.

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:54.450
And the number of young
men we intentionally

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:58.830
had to slaughter in the Sherman
tank, which its shell would

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:01.950
bounce off the Panzer
and the Tiger Tank,

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:05.010
we had to literally
and knowingly sacrifice

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:10.020
an entire frontal attack to be
eviscerated by the German tank

00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:13.680
lines to get enough Shermans
around the back, which

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:15.930
at close range from
behind, was the only way

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:20.370
to kill a Panzer or a
Tiger with a Sherman tank.

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:22.920
And that's because
the people developing

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:26.790
the tank and the airplane,
every extra dollar

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:30.060
was spent on the infantry
and a better gun,

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:31.830
because that was the main event.

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:33.540
The tank was not
meant as a main event,

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:35.880
it was meant to
protect the infantry.

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:37.440
The airplane was
not the main event,

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:40.680
it was to spot troops
for the Signal Corps.

00:15:40.680 --> 00:15:43.500
It was not intended by anybody.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:48.030
The biggest trap of
culture is mindset.

00:15:48.030 --> 00:15:51.210
And we get trapped in a
mindset like electricity,

00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:52.890
that it has to be that way.

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:55.050
Our children will be
plugging into a wall

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:58.590
when the technology does
not need to be that way.

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:01.350
But here's why space is
so much more powerful

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:05.390
and why this question of the
Space Force is so important.

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:08.220
It's because we have
competition today.

00:16:08.220 --> 00:16:11.850
If the development of space
to do these things that I just

00:16:11.850 --> 00:16:17.400
described to you transform
the transportation economy

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:19.710
to be able to deliver anybody
anywhere on planet Earth

00:16:19.710 --> 00:16:23.280
in less than an hour, transform
the energy market where

00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:26.340
everybody can trickle charge
their batteries and capacitors

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:28.470
to power anything on
planet Earth from anywhere

00:16:28.470 --> 00:16:33.000
without any power
lines, any power plants,

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:35.825
transform information where
you can get information

00:16:35.825 --> 00:16:37.200
about what's going
on around you,

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:40.740
and you don't need to be near
a city or near a cell tower,

00:16:40.740 --> 00:16:43.440
because you're delivering it
from a network in space that

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:45.310
can deliver it to
every human being.

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:46.830
And then we can
manufacture things

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:49.980
in space using the
vacuum and zero g,

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:51.780
to not only do
research medically,

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:55.260
but to build facilities
and structures in ways

00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:57.240
we could have never
done before, and deliver

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:58.830
them as light as
a feather anywhere

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:02.310
on planet Earth for pennies on
the dollar of transportation

00:17:02.310 --> 00:17:09.270
costs in a linear sea, land,
and air friction environment.

00:17:09.270 --> 00:17:13.690
And whenever humanity has a
new marketplace like this,

00:17:13.690 --> 00:17:18.180
if there is not some
guardian force that

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:22.109
brings predictability to
that economic marketplace,

00:17:22.109 --> 00:17:24.359
violence ensues.

00:17:24.359 --> 00:17:27.089
Pirates, thieves,
and thugs steal

00:17:27.089 --> 00:17:30.450
what good men and women build.

00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:33.750
And it's just a part
of human nature,

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:35.710
and that will not change.

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:37.320
So as we look to
these new markets

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:40.200
and we see Elon Musk
building a starship that

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:41.910
will be able to
launch from anywhere

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:43.620
and go anywhere in
less than an hour,

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:47.370
with massive volume and
weight, and he throws up

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:50.310
12,000 satellites that will
bring you Wi-Fi from space

00:17:50.310 --> 00:17:53.830
where you will laugh
at your descendants,

00:17:53.830 --> 00:17:58.110
or your fathers and mothers
that had to rely on cell towers,

00:17:58.110 --> 00:18:02.820
or see the little circle of
death waiting for signal,

00:18:02.820 --> 00:18:04.253
they will laugh
and scoff at that.

00:18:04.253 --> 00:18:05.670
They will laugh
and scoff that you

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:09.330
had to put fuel into your tank
in your car or plug into a wall

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:13.770
because your phone was running
out of juice in the airports.

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:18.480
The lines waiting for
the outlet are no more.

00:18:18.480 --> 00:18:21.600
We get trapped in
these paradigms.

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:24.570
But yet, just like
Germany was competition

00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:28.340
for the airplane, the tank,
and the nuclear weapon,

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:32.130
that we eventually
won but at great cost,

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:34.380
China is our competition.

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:36.360
Russia is our competition.

00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:40.260
They see the power of the
economy of space in these four

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:44.820
sectors, and they are
rushing to that future.

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:47.220
And there is no guardian
force in America.

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:48.630
But there is in China.

00:18:48.630 --> 00:18:51.960
China has already
built the organization

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:53.505
and has the strategy
and the doctrine

00:18:53.505 --> 00:18:57.150
and the technology and the
builders for their guardian

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:59.130
force of space.

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:02.430
They are building
a navy in space

00:19:02.430 --> 00:19:04.950
with the equivalent of
battleships and destroyers

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:10.380
that will be able to maneuver
and kill and communicate

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:12.780
with dominance.

00:19:12.780 --> 00:19:14.400
And we are not.

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:23.830
Now, this analogy might
help clarify the picture,

00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:25.780
going back to my original
comment of what's

00:19:25.780 --> 00:19:27.250
really going on here?

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:30.550
The competition is not about
making better satellites,

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:33.670
or even having a
constellation of satellites.

00:19:33.670 --> 00:19:37.720
When you see China on
the far side of the moon,

00:19:37.720 --> 00:19:42.580
mapping today the
minerals and the resources

00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:45.940
so that they can eventually
have infrastructure

00:19:45.940 --> 00:19:49.300
to build and 3D print
and have a manufacturing

00:19:49.300 --> 00:19:52.000
industry in space,
what you are watching

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:55.180
is the equivalent of us sitting
here on our continental United

00:19:55.180 --> 00:19:55.690
States--

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:57.070
let's say we're in Miami.

00:19:57.070 --> 00:19:59.440
And we're looking out
over the wide open ocean.

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:01.910
That ocean is deep space.

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:04.120
The orbit around the
Earth is the shoreline

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:06.340
where the waves are crashing.

00:20:06.340 --> 00:20:08.290
The deep water is space.

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:12.010
And there is a continent
out there three times

00:20:12.010 --> 00:20:14.510
the size of Africa.

00:20:14.510 --> 00:20:15.550
That's the Moon.

00:20:15.550 --> 00:20:17.450
And nobody lives there.

00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:19.000
It's only three days away.

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:21.280
It has massive
amounts of everything

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:22.690
that Mother Earth has.

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:26.170
To include water
on the south pole

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:32.290
and the craters greater than the
Great Lakes, as far as volume.

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:37.600
And China is racing with
ships on that open ocean,

00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:40.670
to that great,
open, desolate place

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:43.690
that can be turned into
resources and blessing

00:20:43.690 --> 00:20:45.940
for a marketplace.

00:20:45.940 --> 00:20:49.180
And they're doing it not
just to get the resources,

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:52.900
but to tap into the trillion
dollar markets on planet Earth.

00:20:52.900 --> 00:20:58.150
Imagine what you could do
if you could sell technology

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:01.510
to somebody from China
and deliver Wi-Fi.

00:21:01.510 --> 00:21:03.670
And once you've built the
infrastructure in space,

00:21:03.670 --> 00:21:06.130
you can deliver it for pennies.

00:21:06.130 --> 00:21:09.370
Electricity, where your
satellite dish doesn't just

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:12.580
get DirecTV now,
it gets energy that

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:14.890
supplies your Chinese
batteries and capacitors

00:21:14.890 --> 00:21:16.630
as they're building.

00:21:16.630 --> 00:21:19.120
To get radio waves
from space that

00:21:19.120 --> 00:21:22.180
give you that energy over time.

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:25.720
They will tap into those
trillion dollar markets

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:29.500
as they have in the past,
as we have in the past,

00:21:29.500 --> 00:21:34.240
and fund their ecosystem, their
economy, their marketplace

00:21:34.240 --> 00:21:37.000
in cislunar space,
which is basically

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:41.620
the distance between the
Earth and the Moon and beyond.

00:21:41.620 --> 00:21:45.880
And we, as an American society,
we are sitting on Miami Beach

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:50.510
sipping our piña colada,
looking out at the waves.

00:21:50.510 --> 00:21:52.710
And as we are
watching China build

00:21:52.710 --> 00:21:56.170
this Navy, with battleships
and destroyers going out

00:21:56.170 --> 00:22:00.100
into the open oceans, and off
to this continent three times

00:22:00.100 --> 00:22:04.870
the size of Africa, we are
building buoys and lighthouses,

00:22:04.870 --> 00:22:07.720
which are the satellites,
that can see and hear

00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:11.290
what's going on, but can't do
a darn thing about that rover

00:22:11.290 --> 00:22:13.882
on the backside of the moon,
the far side of the moon.

00:22:13.882 --> 00:22:15.340
That if we were to
try to go there,

00:22:15.340 --> 00:22:18.320
they could shoot us down.

00:22:18.320 --> 00:22:20.510
And speed matters.

00:22:20.510 --> 00:22:23.900
Speed matters because whoever
gets to the new market

00:22:23.900 --> 00:22:26.090
sets the values for that market.

00:22:26.090 --> 00:22:28.280
And we could either
have the market

00:22:28.280 --> 00:22:29.840
with the values of
our constitution,

00:22:29.840 --> 00:22:32.430
where every human
being is created equal

00:22:32.430 --> 00:22:34.460
and loved equally by
God and their parents

00:22:34.460 --> 00:22:38.990
and their brothers and sisters,
and that respect is manifested

00:22:38.990 --> 00:22:42.740
in the rights of an individual
to vote, to own land,

00:22:42.740 --> 00:22:45.710
to bear arms, all the things
the Constitution gives us.

00:22:45.710 --> 00:22:50.130
Or we can have the values
that we see manifest in China,

00:22:50.130 --> 00:22:52.280
Hong Kong, the Uyghurs.

00:22:52.280 --> 00:22:57.440
You pick your example of
subordination and crushing

00:22:57.440 --> 00:23:01.340
religion and human
rights and human dignity

00:23:01.340 --> 00:23:02.105
and human liberty.

00:23:05.900 --> 00:23:09.260
But America is such a
good-hearted country,

00:23:09.260 --> 00:23:16.050
we oftentimes are deceived by
the nature of China's strategy.

00:23:16.050 --> 00:23:19.700
Their strategy is not to
make better satellites.

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:23.090
Their strategy is to build
an economy before we do.

00:23:23.090 --> 00:23:26.150
Because if you get there
first, they will be able to,

00:23:26.150 --> 00:23:29.120
with a constellation
in space, see and kill

00:23:29.120 --> 00:23:32.600
anything that flies
above the trees.

00:23:32.600 --> 00:23:35.570
The blood and treasure required
to get back to that high ground

00:23:35.570 --> 00:23:38.720
if we are not there
first will pale

00:23:38.720 --> 00:23:41.840
in comparison to World
War II and World War I

00:23:41.840 --> 00:23:44.990
in ways that only those
that study this technology

00:23:44.990 --> 00:23:47.720
and its power can know.

00:23:47.720 --> 00:23:50.030
Because China has met--

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:53.540
for 30 years, they have
met every single milestone

00:23:53.540 --> 00:23:55.330
of their space program.

00:23:55.330 --> 00:23:57.140
And in the next 10
years, they will

00:23:57.140 --> 00:24:01.370
have solar and nuclear power
generation space stations

00:24:01.370 --> 00:24:03.470
on orbit.

00:24:03.470 --> 00:24:06.260
They broadcast that they will
be used for peaceful purposes,

00:24:06.260 --> 00:24:08.240
that those radio waves
will bring energy

00:24:08.240 --> 00:24:11.000
to anybody on planet Earth
without the need for power

00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:14.090
lines or power plants.

00:24:14.090 --> 00:24:17.210
But in a millisecond,
that dominance

00:24:17.210 --> 00:24:19.400
of the electromagnetic
spectrum can

00:24:19.400 --> 00:24:23.420
be directed energy that could
paralyze any part of our power

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:27.290
grid and freeze any
military might that America

00:24:27.290 --> 00:24:29.420
builds on the spot.

00:24:29.420 --> 00:24:32.540
Every carrier battle fleet
is a cork in the water.

00:24:32.540 --> 00:24:35.870
Every fleet of fighters
is dead on the ramp,

00:24:35.870 --> 00:24:39.860
can't even turn the wheel
because of our vulnerability.

00:24:39.860 --> 00:24:44.180
China has openly stated they
are weaponizing everything

00:24:44.180 --> 00:24:46.070
Western civilization
was built on--

00:24:46.070 --> 00:24:48.290
energy and information.

00:24:48.290 --> 00:24:50.520
And 5G is a perfect example.

00:24:50.520 --> 00:24:52.820
If you don't think they
will act in a way that

00:24:52.820 --> 00:24:55.160
steals our ideas
and our technology,

00:24:55.160 --> 00:24:58.130
duplicates it, and then
dominates the marketplace,

00:24:58.130 --> 00:24:59.300
take a look at 5G.

00:24:59.300 --> 00:25:02.600
Nobody 20 years ago
would have ever believed

00:25:02.600 --> 00:25:05.690
that America would not
have an answer to 5G when

00:25:05.690 --> 00:25:08.810
China rolled it out.

00:25:08.810 --> 00:25:10.080
Why didn't we have it?

00:25:10.080 --> 00:25:11.990
Well, it's pretty easy.

00:25:11.990 --> 00:25:16.550
China invited companies like
Lucent Technology, Motorola,

00:25:16.550 --> 00:25:20.300
Nortel, into China
with a nice package

00:25:20.300 --> 00:25:26.910
of benefits at the cost of
proprietary information,

00:25:26.910 --> 00:25:28.790
intellectual property.

00:25:28.790 --> 00:25:31.970
And they built Huawei out
of the bankrupt carcasses

00:25:31.970 --> 00:25:35.820
of those three companies.

00:25:35.820 --> 00:25:38.580
They stole the technology,
they duplicated it,

00:25:38.580 --> 00:25:41.610
and then they dominated the
marketplace in an unfair way.

00:25:41.610 --> 00:25:46.560
Unfair perfect example,
Vietnam in 2006.

00:25:46.560 --> 00:25:48.360
They were bidding
for companies to come

00:25:48.360 --> 00:25:50.910
build their telecommunication
infrastructure.

00:25:50.910 --> 00:25:55.170
And so all these companies that
were world class global leaders

00:25:55.170 --> 00:25:59.890
in telecommunications put out
their bids, competitive bids.

00:25:59.890 --> 00:26:02.760
Huawei's bid, as a
young company being

00:26:02.760 --> 00:26:06.000
grown by the Communist Party?

00:26:06.000 --> 00:26:07.350
Zero dollars.

00:26:07.350 --> 00:26:08.680
They built it for free.

00:26:08.680 --> 00:26:10.230
How do you compete with that?

00:26:10.230 --> 00:26:13.930
The same thing is happening with
the space industry right now.

00:26:13.930 --> 00:26:19.793
If you're a German
that wants a satellite,

00:26:19.793 --> 00:26:21.210
China will give
it to you for free

00:26:21.210 --> 00:26:23.210
if you buy their satellite,
and they'll give you

00:26:23.210 --> 00:26:25.020
the launch for 90% discount.

00:26:25.020 --> 00:26:27.960
Far below what the
market can bear.

00:26:27.960 --> 00:26:31.230
Because they can funnel
their political focus,

00:26:31.230 --> 00:26:34.500
their military focus,
and their financial focus

00:26:34.500 --> 00:26:37.290
into a vision and a
plan that does not

00:26:37.290 --> 00:26:39.870
suffer from the blessing
of our republic,

00:26:39.870 --> 00:26:43.270
where parties come and
go, programs get crushed,

00:26:43.270 --> 00:26:45.870
they come back, and you can't
plan one year to the other,

00:26:45.870 --> 00:26:48.078
or some years you can't plan
it all with a continuing

00:26:48.078 --> 00:26:50.257
resolution, where you
can't do anything new.

00:26:50.257 --> 00:26:51.840
And you don't have
any money to do it.

00:26:54.640 --> 00:26:57.960
This is the difference
in strategy.

00:26:57.960 --> 00:27:01.850
A strategy of speed to get to
this new continent of wealth

00:27:01.850 --> 00:27:06.540
called the Moon and asteroids
and a cislunar economy,

00:27:06.540 --> 00:27:11.651
to bring power to whatever
country dominates that economy.

00:27:14.420 --> 00:27:17.990
It's like America
is a race car that

00:27:17.990 --> 00:27:21.045
has been winning races for
70 years since World War II.

00:27:21.045 --> 00:27:22.670
We're going 90 miles
an hour, and we've

00:27:22.670 --> 00:27:25.460
done it that way
since World War II.

00:27:25.460 --> 00:27:30.120
It's our entire mindset, our
entire lives the same way.

00:27:30.120 --> 00:27:33.530
China is in a car
right behind us.

00:27:33.530 --> 00:27:38.570
The car isn't as good, but
it's going 120 miles an hour.

00:27:38.570 --> 00:27:42.800
We can say today, we
are dominant in space.

00:27:42.800 --> 00:27:45.800
But the trend lines is
what you have to look at.

00:27:45.800 --> 00:27:47.750
And they will pass us
in the next few years

00:27:47.750 --> 00:27:49.260
if we do not do something.

00:27:49.260 --> 00:27:52.010
And they will win this race, and
then they will put roadblocks

00:27:52.010 --> 00:27:54.110
up to space.

00:27:54.110 --> 00:27:56.360
Because once you get the
ultimate high ground,

00:27:56.360 --> 00:28:00.530
that strategic high
ground, it's curtains

00:28:00.530 --> 00:28:03.200
for anybody trying to get to
that high ground behind them.

00:28:03.200 --> 00:28:09.430
Because they can apply power,
maneuver, and communication

00:28:09.430 --> 00:28:12.710
at infinitesimally
lower price points.

00:28:12.710 --> 00:28:15.140
And ultimately,
everything is economic.

00:28:15.140 --> 00:28:17.730
If you can do something
cheaper than I can do it,

00:28:17.730 --> 00:28:19.970
you will eventually beat me.

00:28:19.970 --> 00:28:24.090
And all national security
comes from economies.

00:28:24.090 --> 00:28:26.300
So speed is essential.

00:28:26.300 --> 00:28:29.120
So we are building
brilliant satellites.

00:28:29.120 --> 00:28:32.360
We are building
brilliant commands.

00:28:32.360 --> 00:28:36.530
But we will be like taking
a glorified knife to a tank

00:28:36.530 --> 00:28:41.810
fight, or the perfect single
action rifle to a machine gun

00:28:41.810 --> 00:28:43.100
fight.

00:28:43.100 --> 00:28:47.390
Because of this strategy is
not fighting China's strategy,

00:28:47.390 --> 00:28:51.290
and we are stuck in our
mindset of the last 70 years

00:28:51.290 --> 00:28:53.780
and what space has done so far.

00:28:53.780 --> 00:28:56.990
This is not a military race,
this is an economic race.

00:28:56.990 --> 00:28:59.300
And if you do not have a
guardian force to bring

00:28:59.300 --> 00:29:01.910
rule of law and predictability,
no venture capitalists

00:29:01.910 --> 00:29:03.890
will know how to
make risk decisions.

00:29:03.890 --> 00:29:05.900
No company will
be able to invest.

00:29:05.900 --> 00:29:09.770
And those that do will have
their hard work stolen away,

00:29:09.770 --> 00:29:15.260
because the rule of law is not
codified by a guardian force.

00:29:15.260 --> 00:29:19.490
The good news is, there are
more societies on planet Earth

00:29:19.490 --> 00:29:22.550
that share our values as
an American society, that

00:29:22.550 --> 00:29:24.420
will work with us to do this.

00:29:24.420 --> 00:29:27.860
But right now, we're paralyzed.

00:29:27.860 --> 00:29:29.900
Look at what's happening
in our government.

00:29:29.900 --> 00:29:34.860
Yes, argument is good,
but we are paralyzed.

00:29:34.860 --> 00:29:38.810
This National Defense
Authorization Act is at risk.

00:29:38.810 --> 00:29:44.870
And even though
this president was

00:29:44.870 --> 00:29:52.910
able to get a space force into
the dialogue, when he first

00:29:52.910 --> 00:29:58.200
said it, the bureaucracy
howled with resistance.

00:29:58.200 --> 00:30:02.970
And only after a year
and a half of hard work

00:30:02.970 --> 00:30:04.040
are they now on board.

00:30:04.040 --> 00:30:07.730
Just an example of the
resistance to the status quo,

00:30:07.730 --> 00:30:10.490
wanting the status quo
to stay what it is.

00:30:10.490 --> 00:30:14.860
But it's ironic, because it
reminds me of a story in 1400

00:30:14.860 --> 00:30:17.870
that is an example that there's
nothing new under the sun

00:30:17.870 --> 00:30:20.900
and history may not repeat
itself, but it sure does rhyme.

00:30:20.900 --> 00:30:25.340
That old saying that
is clever but true.

00:30:25.340 --> 00:30:32.300
In 1400, China had a two
party system, Ming dynasty.

00:30:32.300 --> 00:30:36.590
The party in power saw this
thing called a navy and said,

00:30:36.590 --> 00:30:41.060
that is powerful,
because that navy fleet

00:30:41.060 --> 00:30:44.150
will mean that the ocean is
not a barrier, but rather

00:30:44.150 --> 00:30:46.250
a highway to new marketplaces.

00:30:46.250 --> 00:30:49.550
And they built the biggest
navy on planet Earth.

00:30:49.550 --> 00:30:52.460
They would have been
the England of 1400

00:30:52.460 --> 00:30:54.140
had they finished the job.

00:30:54.140 --> 00:30:57.560
But the bickering of
politics, when the new party

00:30:57.560 --> 00:31:02.330
came into power, they
burned every ship

00:31:02.330 --> 00:31:07.640
to the ground in spite,
because the other party's idea

00:31:07.640 --> 00:31:10.700
was the idea for a
navy, and not theirs.

00:31:10.700 --> 00:31:15.590
That began a 600 year journey
to the century of humiliation.

00:31:15.590 --> 00:31:18.380
And I'm here to tell you,
I read every document

00:31:18.380 --> 00:31:19.760
that comes out of China.

00:31:19.760 --> 00:31:23.750
I read every speech by every
senior policy official.

00:31:23.750 --> 00:31:27.050
And I will tell you, they
talk about this story.

00:31:27.050 --> 00:31:29.150
And that the Middle
Kingdom is back,

00:31:29.150 --> 00:31:30.830
and America is in
its crosshairs.

00:31:30.830 --> 00:31:35.330
And space is the navy for
the 21st century economy,

00:31:35.330 --> 00:31:37.910
a networked economy
that will dominate

00:31:37.910 --> 00:31:42.500
any linear terrestrial economy
in the four engines of growth

00:31:42.500 --> 00:31:44.960
and dominance that
change world power--

00:31:44.960 --> 00:31:49.340
transportation, information,
energy, and manufacturing.

00:31:49.340 --> 00:31:51.710
And they are building
that infrastructure,

00:31:51.710 --> 00:31:54.110
they are unapologetic
about it, and they

00:31:54.110 --> 00:31:58.680
plan on declaring victory as the
dominant world power in space

00:31:58.680 --> 00:32:04.950
at the 100 year
anniversary, 2049.

00:32:04.950 --> 00:32:10.160
And in the next 10 years,
their energy and space

00:32:10.160 --> 00:32:12.100
with nuclear and
solar power that

00:32:12.100 --> 00:32:13.850
can be beamed to
the earth for good

00:32:13.850 --> 00:32:18.140
and for bad, their ability
to control gateways of 5G

00:32:18.140 --> 00:32:22.760
using space, quantum, artificial
intelligence, supercomputing,

00:32:22.760 --> 00:32:25.330
to be able to shape the
perception of the world

00:32:25.330 --> 00:32:28.430
and to tell any story
and to lie about America

00:32:28.430 --> 00:32:32.930
or anybody else that is
counter to their purpose.

00:32:32.930 --> 00:32:36.110
And you see how our
interdependency as a world

00:32:36.110 --> 00:32:39.680
plays out when China
can lie about America

00:32:39.680 --> 00:32:44.000
to all global markets, and
how that affects our economy

00:32:44.000 --> 00:32:45.980
and our stock market.

00:32:45.980 --> 00:32:48.440
Ultimately, it is
the manifestation

00:32:48.440 --> 00:32:53.750
of a long, patient plan to
dominate information and energy

00:32:53.750 --> 00:32:57.290
as weapons against the West,
so China's Middle Kingdom

00:32:57.290 --> 00:32:59.720
can come back.

00:32:59.720 --> 00:33:04.010
This is why we
need a space force.

00:33:04.010 --> 00:33:06.710
This is why it needs to be now.

00:33:06.710 --> 00:33:09.590
Because if we fumble the
football politically this year,

00:33:09.590 --> 00:33:13.040
it'll be two years before we
get another National Defense

00:33:13.040 --> 00:33:16.380
Authorization Act that will
give this the chance to survive.

00:33:16.380 --> 00:33:19.610
And that's two years of money
in the bank at compound interest

00:33:19.610 --> 00:33:22.490
for China, who's
furiously swimming away

00:33:22.490 --> 00:33:24.590
to that continent
of Africa as we're

00:33:24.590 --> 00:33:28.550
sitting on the beaches of Miami,
admiring the tide and our buoys

00:33:28.550 --> 00:33:30.800
and lighthouses that can
see exactly what's going

00:33:30.800 --> 00:33:33.200
on the shoreline in our orbit.

00:33:37.780 --> 00:33:39.970
Why do we need a space force?

00:33:39.970 --> 00:33:42.670
Because it's an
economic competition

00:33:42.670 --> 00:33:44.470
for the values of the future.

00:33:44.470 --> 00:33:45.580
When do we need it?

00:33:45.580 --> 00:33:46.540
Now.

00:33:46.540 --> 00:33:48.380
What does it need to do?

00:33:48.380 --> 00:33:52.450
It doesn't have to have
war fighting capability.

00:33:52.450 --> 00:33:55.960
It has to be able to defend
the economy of space.

00:33:55.960 --> 00:34:00.130
A Coast Guard, a Merchant
Marine for space.

00:34:00.130 --> 00:34:03.760
Because the national security
muscles and capabilities

00:34:03.760 --> 00:34:08.469
will flow easily once
we tap into the profits

00:34:08.469 --> 00:34:10.570
of those marketplaces.

00:34:10.570 --> 00:34:13.000
Just like we have a
strong navy, because we

00:34:13.000 --> 00:34:15.580
have a strong shipbuilding
industry, and a strong Merchant

00:34:15.580 --> 00:34:18.159
Marine, and just because
we have a strong Air Force.

00:34:18.159 --> 00:34:21.159
Because the aerospace
industry is our largest export

00:34:21.159 --> 00:34:22.330
as a nation.

00:34:22.330 --> 00:34:27.110
This is what long term strategy
and economic power look like,

00:34:27.110 --> 00:34:30.489
and this is what we need.

00:34:30.489 --> 00:34:32.350
And the scientists,
engineers, historians,

00:34:32.350 --> 00:34:36.080
and strategists of our age have
brought this to our government.

00:34:36.080 --> 00:34:38.110
The government has said, do it.

00:34:38.110 --> 00:34:41.210
And now Congress is
asking the question,

00:34:41.210 --> 00:34:43.540
why do we need to spend
money on a space force?

00:34:43.540 --> 00:34:46.130
It would be like Teddy Roosevelt
getting pushback saying,

00:34:46.130 --> 00:34:48.310
why do we need a Panama Canal?

00:34:48.310 --> 00:34:51.250
Why do we need an Eisenhower
interstate system?

00:34:51.250 --> 00:34:53.630
It's for commerce.

00:34:53.630 --> 00:34:57.160
The power of the perpetuation
of the American dream

00:34:57.160 --> 00:34:58.810
and the American values.

00:34:58.810 --> 00:35:01.150
You are at a pivotal point.

00:35:01.150 --> 00:35:03.460
The American people
don't know this story.

00:35:03.460 --> 00:35:05.680
Congress doesn't even know
this story adequately,

00:35:05.680 --> 00:35:08.120
except for a few.

00:35:08.120 --> 00:35:10.960
And if we don't
get this story out,

00:35:10.960 --> 00:35:14.452
your grandchildren will
probably be speaking Chinese.

00:35:14.452 --> 00:35:16.660
That's not a bad language,
because the Chinese people

00:35:16.660 --> 00:35:18.010
are beautiful people.

00:35:18.010 --> 00:35:22.420
But their Communist Party will
murder the future generations

00:35:22.420 --> 00:35:23.560
of free-loving people.

00:35:23.560 --> 00:35:27.400
Liberty can be snuffed
out if we are not

00:35:27.400 --> 00:35:30.490
mindful of the
power of technology

00:35:30.490 --> 00:35:35.320
and the trap of a mindset
that clings to the status quo,

00:35:35.320 --> 00:35:37.390
instead of allowing
our engineers

00:35:37.390 --> 00:35:39.520
and our inventors
and our marketplaces

00:35:39.520 --> 00:35:42.700
build a new future
with new paradigms

00:35:42.700 --> 00:35:47.310
to dominate the marketplaces
of the 21st century.

00:35:47.310 --> 00:35:49.060
Thank you for your
time and for listening,

00:35:49.060 --> 00:35:50.602
and I look forward
to your questions.

00:35:50.602 --> 00:35:53.530
[APPLAUSE]

00:36:01.220 --> 00:36:04.857
See, that speech you wrote
was awesome, Michael.

00:36:04.857 --> 00:36:07.190
MICHAEL ANTON: My question
is rhetorical, which is we've

00:36:07.190 --> 00:36:13.160
seen a lot of news lately
about career officers, Foreign

00:36:13.160 --> 00:36:15.650
Service officers, so-called
deep staters in the National

00:36:15.650 --> 00:36:16.717
Security Council.

00:36:16.717 --> 00:36:18.050
I have my misgivings about that.

00:36:18.050 --> 00:36:19.883
But then I ask, if we're
going to have them,

00:36:19.883 --> 00:36:22.000
why can't we have this guy?

00:36:22.000 --> 00:36:26.000
OK, questions and there are
microphones roving around.

00:36:26.000 --> 00:36:29.135
So please wait until you are
handed a mic before you ask.

00:36:29.135 --> 00:36:30.510
STEVEN QUAST: So
the audience can

00:36:30.510 --> 00:36:32.895
you hear the question
and people online.

00:36:32.895 --> 00:36:34.250
AUDIENCE: Sure.

00:36:34.250 --> 00:36:35.030
Pardon me.

00:36:35.030 --> 00:36:37.880
Could you describe
the nature of--

00:36:37.880 --> 00:36:40.220
this August, the SAP
level almost immediately.

00:36:40.220 --> 00:36:42.950
But for everybody's
edification, could you

00:36:42.950 --> 00:36:46.310
describe our offensive
and defensive capabilities

00:36:46.310 --> 00:36:48.890
in space versus those that our
adversaries currently have,

00:36:48.890 --> 00:36:51.250
and what they will have
in the very near future?

00:36:51.250 --> 00:36:53.460
STEVEN QUAST: OK, so
everybody heard that question.

00:36:53.460 --> 00:36:56.720
I will tell you that whether
you're an Army officer,

00:36:56.720 --> 00:36:58.650
a Naval officer or
an Air Force officer

00:36:58.650 --> 00:37:03.550
or a Coast Guard officer, a
Marine officer, doesn't matter.

00:37:03.550 --> 00:37:07.260
There is one truth
about a new domain.

00:37:07.260 --> 00:37:10.300
If you want to dominate it and
you want to bring rule of law,

00:37:10.300 --> 00:37:12.000
you have to be able
to maneuver more

00:37:12.000 --> 00:37:14.040
aggressively and at
cheaper price points

00:37:14.040 --> 00:37:15.390
than your competition.

00:37:15.390 --> 00:37:17.790
You have to be
able to communicate

00:37:17.790 --> 00:37:21.810
more ubiquitously
and more resiliently

00:37:21.810 --> 00:37:23.040
than your competition.

00:37:23.040 --> 00:37:27.720
And you have to be able
to bring power to bear,

00:37:27.720 --> 00:37:31.440
whether that's kinetic
power, informational power,

00:37:31.440 --> 00:37:33.038
non-kinetic power.

00:37:33.038 --> 00:37:34.830
You have to be able to
bring power to bear,

00:37:34.830 --> 00:37:38.250
and you have to do all of those
three things cheaper and faster

00:37:38.250 --> 00:37:40.220
than your competition.

00:37:40.220 --> 00:37:42.720
And you have to be able to deny
your competition those three

00:37:42.720 --> 00:37:44.460
things.

00:37:44.460 --> 00:37:49.230
China is feverishly working
on those three components

00:37:49.230 --> 00:37:52.080
to be applied outside
of the gravity well.

00:37:52.080 --> 00:37:55.050
That's beyond the orbits into
the moon and the cislunar

00:37:55.050 --> 00:37:58.380
space, using the sun as
their source of energy that

00:37:58.380 --> 00:38:03.700
is perpetual and can be beamed
to any place in that ecosystem.

00:38:03.700 --> 00:38:05.970
They are literally
building the coal stations

00:38:05.970 --> 00:38:08.190
equivalent to the ones
we built in the Pacific

00:38:08.190 --> 00:38:11.570
when Teddy Roosevelt built the
great white fleet with iron

00:38:11.570 --> 00:38:12.820
ships instead of wooden ships.

00:38:12.820 --> 00:38:14.820
In fact, that story
is another one.

00:38:14.820 --> 00:38:17.730
The wooden shipbuilders
and the sail builders

00:38:17.730 --> 00:38:19.830
did not want to let
go of the wooden ship.

00:38:19.830 --> 00:38:23.130
It was better than these
stinky old iron ships.

00:38:23.130 --> 00:38:26.190
That was another journey
of a new paradigm that

00:38:26.190 --> 00:38:27.880
had to crush an old paradigm.

00:38:27.880 --> 00:38:29.190
And it was hard and long.

00:38:29.190 --> 00:38:30.670
So I will tell you this.

00:38:30.670 --> 00:38:33.360
Everything I've said
is in the open press.

00:38:33.360 --> 00:38:36.960
But much of it has to be
translated from Mandarin.

00:38:36.960 --> 00:38:39.900
And that's another
problem our journalists

00:38:39.900 --> 00:38:43.600
and our American public have an
understanding what's going on.

00:38:43.600 --> 00:38:47.430
But I will tell you this, 33
years of studying technology,

00:38:47.430 --> 00:38:51.450
the Chinese, culture,
history, human nature,

00:38:51.450 --> 00:38:55.320
China is feverishly
developing capability

00:38:55.320 --> 00:39:02.610
to dominate those three areas in
cislunar space, and we are not.

00:39:02.610 --> 00:39:08.580
We are perfecting orbital
mechanics, the shore line work,

00:39:08.580 --> 00:39:13.560
precision, quality, brilliant
capability and equipment,

00:39:13.560 --> 00:39:15.630
but irrelevant to China.

00:39:15.630 --> 00:39:17.310
They can maneuver
outside the gravity

00:39:17.310 --> 00:39:19.590
well, around the
backside of the moon.

00:39:19.590 --> 00:39:21.870
And there is nothing
we can do if we are not

00:39:21.870 --> 00:39:26.380
dominant in that
geography as well.

00:39:26.380 --> 00:39:29.430
So that's why the Space Force is
so urgent, because China's got

00:39:29.430 --> 00:39:30.750
a head start.

00:39:30.750 --> 00:39:34.590
That car, right on our bumper,
going 120 miles an hour,

00:39:34.590 --> 00:39:36.360
it won't be better
than what we'll build,

00:39:36.360 --> 00:39:38.820
because we have an open
market free economy.

00:39:38.820 --> 00:39:40.770
Ideas flourish.

00:39:40.770 --> 00:39:45.300
But China steals them so fast,
duplicates them so rapidly,

00:39:45.300 --> 00:39:51.480
floods a market so insidiously,
that even the brilliant idea

00:39:51.480 --> 00:39:53.640
like what Tesla did
with their battery

00:39:53.640 --> 00:39:56.640
that China stole and duplicated,
even a brilliant idea

00:39:56.640 --> 00:39:58.590
like that, we're
behind the power curve.

00:39:58.590 --> 00:39:59.670
5G.

00:39:59.670 --> 00:40:03.210
We have no answer, because China
took all our stuff, built it,

00:40:03.210 --> 00:40:05.070
flooded the market.

00:40:05.070 --> 00:40:07.130
And now if you're a company
that doesn't have 5G,

00:40:07.130 --> 00:40:12.170
you can't compete because speed
is life in the 21st century.

00:40:12.170 --> 00:40:13.590
And we don't have an answer.

00:40:13.590 --> 00:40:15.140
Germany wants it.

00:40:15.140 --> 00:40:18.330
We would love as an American
country to give them some 5G

00:40:18.330 --> 00:40:20.760
with the values of
America behind it.

00:40:20.760 --> 00:40:25.210
But they only have one
option, and that's China.

00:40:25.210 --> 00:40:26.700
Yeah.

00:40:26.700 --> 00:40:28.200
I'll let you decide who goes.

00:40:28.200 --> 00:40:28.950
MICHAEL ANTON: OK.

00:40:28.950 --> 00:40:29.930
Right there.

00:40:29.930 --> 00:40:30.776
Yeah.

00:40:30.776 --> 00:40:34.430
STEVEN QUAST: Sorry, she is much
better looking than you are.

00:40:34.430 --> 00:40:35.430
That's all I got to say.

00:40:35.430 --> 00:40:37.410
AUDIENCE: Thank you so
much for your speech.

00:40:37.410 --> 00:40:39.850
I'm also one of the
WHIP students here.

00:40:39.850 --> 00:40:42.750
And my question is, you've
talked a lot about the two

00:40:42.750 --> 00:40:46.160
competing paradigms, how there's
the old one and the new one.

00:40:46.160 --> 00:40:48.762
And the famous scientific
philosopher Thomas Kuhn often

00:40:48.762 --> 00:40:50.220
spoke about how
these paradigms are

00:40:50.220 --> 00:40:52.290
incommensurable to
each other, meaning

00:40:52.290 --> 00:40:54.000
that if you're in
one paradigm, you

00:40:54.000 --> 00:40:57.510
can't understand what someone's
saying from another paradigm.

00:40:57.510 --> 00:40:59.760
How do you propose
that we bridge that gap

00:40:59.760 --> 00:41:02.670
to bring people from the
old way of viewing things

00:41:02.670 --> 00:41:05.130
into the new way in a
manner that's effective,

00:41:05.130 --> 00:41:07.397
and that helps us spread
our values around the world?

00:41:07.397 --> 00:41:08.980
STEVEN QUAST: That's
a great question,

00:41:08.980 --> 00:41:11.430
and this is something that
I'm so glad you asked,

00:41:11.430 --> 00:41:16.050
because history gives us all
the answers to this question.

00:41:16.050 --> 00:41:20.610
And one of the reasons why I
was fortunate enough to see this

00:41:20.610 --> 00:41:22.830
is because I grew up in a
different world paradigm.

00:41:22.830 --> 00:41:25.440
I was raised in a tribe, I
didn't have to go to school.

00:41:25.440 --> 00:41:27.270
Which explains a
lot, by the way,

00:41:27.270 --> 00:41:30.480
still can't write
or spell very well.

00:41:30.480 --> 00:41:32.730
And then coming to a
different world paradigm

00:41:32.730 --> 00:41:35.460
at a fragile young
age allowed me

00:41:35.460 --> 00:41:38.460
to see how devastating
the communication

00:41:38.460 --> 00:41:40.620
gap can be between paradigms.

00:41:40.620 --> 00:41:44.520
And we as civilizations
build a paradigm like energy,

00:41:44.520 --> 00:41:46.650
let's say, the electricity
that we have delivered.

00:41:46.650 --> 00:41:49.140
And we squirrel away at
inventing and innovating

00:41:49.140 --> 00:41:52.065
within that paradigm, and
nobody looks outside to say,

00:41:52.065 --> 00:41:53.940
hey, is there a different
economic curve here

00:41:53.940 --> 00:41:55.470
we can jump to?

00:41:55.470 --> 00:41:57.900
But there are enough
people in our society

00:41:57.900 --> 00:41:59.400
that know how to
jump to that curve.

00:41:59.400 --> 00:42:02.365
Elon Musk, Jeff Bezos,
Richard Branson.

00:42:02.365 --> 00:42:05.142
God rest his soul, Paul Allen.

00:42:05.142 --> 00:42:07.350
Luckily they have the money
to actually do something,

00:42:07.350 --> 00:42:10.190
but they were rebels,
they were mavericks.

00:42:10.190 --> 00:42:15.320
They were ridiculed
until they proved it.

00:42:15.320 --> 00:42:20.240
So this is this played out with
Franklin Delano Roosevelt. When

00:42:20.240 --> 00:42:22.820
we saw that Germany
was pursuing the bomb,

00:42:22.820 --> 00:42:24.710
and we knew that if they
got that bomb first,

00:42:24.710 --> 00:42:27.950
it was intuitive that
we had to be fast,

00:42:27.950 --> 00:42:30.380
FDR did not turn to the
bureaucracy of the Army

00:42:30.380 --> 00:42:31.880
and say, build me
a bomb, because he

00:42:31.880 --> 00:42:36.050
knew the status quo and the
bureaucratic organizations

00:42:36.050 --> 00:42:38.810
never can jump out
of their paradigm.

00:42:38.810 --> 00:42:41.300
The pig does not
slaughter itself, OK?

00:42:41.300 --> 00:42:42.530
You have to get outsiders.

00:42:42.530 --> 00:42:44.510
That's why Congress and
the Executive Branch

00:42:44.510 --> 00:42:47.390
have always been the ones that
have changed the military, not

00:42:47.390 --> 00:42:49.190
inside.

00:42:49.190 --> 00:42:51.800
So what FDR did is he
found the right leader.

00:42:51.800 --> 00:42:53.870
And that was Oppenheimer.

00:42:53.870 --> 00:42:55.910
Eisenhower did the same thing.

00:42:55.910 --> 00:42:59.510
As the Soviet Union was
rearing its ugly head,

00:42:59.510 --> 00:43:02.510
and the army was suggesting
putting a million soldiers

00:43:02.510 --> 00:43:05.690
with bayonets affixed in the
fold, the gap of Germany,

00:43:05.690 --> 00:43:07.490
Eisenhower said no.

00:43:07.490 --> 00:43:10.970
Because one tactical nuke will
kill all my sons and daughters,

00:43:10.970 --> 00:43:12.830
and I can't afford it.

00:43:12.830 --> 00:43:16.190
And he turned to two
innovators, General Shriver

00:43:16.190 --> 00:43:17.210
and Admiral Rickover.

00:43:17.210 --> 00:43:21.920
And he said, build me a nuclear
triad so we can have a balance.

00:43:21.920 --> 00:43:23.570
Now, mutually
assured destruction

00:43:23.570 --> 00:43:26.070
is no happy way of
going through life.

00:43:26.070 --> 00:43:28.670
But it was a way
of having a bulwark

00:43:28.670 --> 00:43:32.810
against this
devastating technology.

00:43:32.810 --> 00:43:34.730
The same is true today.

00:43:34.730 --> 00:43:38.050
We need a Manhattan
type project in order

00:43:38.050 --> 00:43:39.440
to develop this properly.

00:43:39.440 --> 00:43:41.320
Because the price
of entry to space

00:43:41.320 --> 00:43:43.750
is so high that
only billionaires

00:43:43.750 --> 00:43:46.480
that are willing to pour
their own money into it

00:43:46.480 --> 00:43:47.590
are making any progress.

00:43:47.590 --> 00:43:51.250
But they are hounded and
blocked at every turn.

00:43:51.250 --> 00:43:53.840
Elon Musk, for example,
has to pay the Air Force

00:43:53.840 --> 00:43:56.890
$13 million every time he
launches from Vandenberg Air

00:43:56.890 --> 00:43:59.410
Force Base for no good reason.

00:43:59.410 --> 00:44:01.550
Just risk aversion
in a bureaucracy.

00:44:01.550 --> 00:44:02.980
And when everything
goes perfect,

00:44:02.980 --> 00:44:04.970
he doesn't get that money back.

00:44:04.970 --> 00:44:07.400
They use it for their own
coffers and their own thing.

00:44:07.400 --> 00:44:10.840
That's the cover your butt
kind of mentality that happens

00:44:10.840 --> 00:44:14.350
in a bureaucracy that cannot
jump outside of the paradigm.

00:44:14.350 --> 00:44:15.730
There's no other way.

00:44:15.730 --> 00:44:18.520
Turning to the government or
the bureaucracy to do this

00:44:18.520 --> 00:44:19.850
will not work.

00:44:19.850 --> 00:44:21.820
But an Executive
Branch or a Congress

00:44:21.820 --> 00:44:24.670
that's willing to pick the
right leader that understands

00:44:24.670 --> 00:44:28.180
that technology, the history,
the culture, the paradigm,

00:44:28.180 --> 00:44:31.600
and picks the right
engineers and scientists,

00:44:31.600 --> 00:44:32.710
they'll build it.

00:44:32.710 --> 00:44:36.070
Because there's nothing more
powerful than the American free

00:44:36.070 --> 00:44:39.610
enterprise that welcomes
diversity of thought

00:44:39.610 --> 00:44:42.040
and will try things and fail.

00:44:42.040 --> 00:44:47.030
And no Communist Party is going
to shoot them if they fail.

00:44:47.030 --> 00:44:49.840
If they fail for the right
reasons, they are promoted.

00:44:49.840 --> 00:44:52.250
If they fail for the wrong
reasons, you coach them,

00:44:52.250 --> 00:44:56.330
and if they fail three
times, you fire them.

00:44:56.330 --> 00:44:58.130
For example, General
Shriver, as he

00:44:58.130 --> 00:45:01.010
was building the missile
fields of our nuclear triad,

00:45:01.010 --> 00:45:04.400
the first 13 rockets blew up.

00:45:04.400 --> 00:45:07.100
Only Eisenhower was
able to protect him

00:45:07.100 --> 00:45:09.440
from the hounds of Congress
and the Air Force that

00:45:09.440 --> 00:45:12.410
hated him, that wanted
him out, that felt

00:45:12.410 --> 00:45:16.820
that his work was coming at
the cost of the man bomber.

00:45:16.820 --> 00:45:19.820
History is playing out again.

00:45:19.820 --> 00:45:22.950
Did that answer your question?

00:45:22.950 --> 00:45:23.872
Who's next?

00:45:23.872 --> 00:45:24.796
MICHAEL ANTON: You.

00:45:24.796 --> 00:45:26.115
Go ahead.

00:45:26.115 --> 00:45:27.490
STEVEN QUAST: Your
mic is coming.

00:45:30.661 --> 00:45:34.300
AUDIENCE: Hi, I'm Jacob
Rich from Reason Foundation.

00:45:34.300 --> 00:45:36.120
And I'm curious.

00:45:36.120 --> 00:45:38.290
So you said that
China's already started

00:45:38.290 --> 00:45:42.430
building destroyers and other
military vessels for space.

00:45:42.430 --> 00:45:44.650
And I'm just curious,
should we steal

00:45:44.650 --> 00:45:46.612
their intellectual
property to catch up?

00:45:46.612 --> 00:45:48.070
STEVEN QUAST: Well,
I will tell you

00:45:48.070 --> 00:45:50.980
that this is the insidious
nature of strategy

00:45:50.980 --> 00:45:52.140
versus equipment.

00:45:52.140 --> 00:45:53.740
OK?

00:45:53.740 --> 00:45:58.000
So China is building nuclear
thermal power propulsion

00:45:58.000 --> 00:46:01.540
capabilities to be able
to maneuver in space.

00:46:01.540 --> 00:46:04.780
We know how to do that,
and we can do it better.

00:46:04.780 --> 00:46:06.740
Their stuff is not good.

00:46:06.740 --> 00:46:07.960
Now, 5G is good.

00:46:07.960 --> 00:46:11.428
The 5G technology is good,
because it's our stuff.

00:46:11.428 --> 00:46:12.970
But the stuff they're
building is not

00:46:12.970 --> 00:46:14.680
better than what we can build.

00:46:14.680 --> 00:46:16.173
It's not about equipment.

00:46:16.173 --> 00:46:17.590
It's not about
stealing our ideas,

00:46:17.590 --> 00:46:19.910
because their ideas
are inferior to ours.

00:46:19.910 --> 00:46:23.770
It's the fact that they're
building an entire method

00:46:23.770 --> 00:46:28.120
of being able to have a blanket
of power over America in space

00:46:28.120 --> 00:46:31.600
that can bring directed energy
to paralyze our power grids,

00:46:31.600 --> 00:46:37.360
paralyze our cars, paralyze our
military, disrupt our markets.

00:46:37.360 --> 00:46:40.270
They're doing it on a social
level with the Confucius

00:46:40.270 --> 00:46:42.420
Centers and a narrative.

00:46:42.420 --> 00:46:44.320
The small space
companies, for example, I

00:46:44.320 --> 00:46:46.720
could bring in the CEOs of
the small space companies,

00:46:46.720 --> 00:46:48.400
and here's what's
happening to them.

00:46:48.400 --> 00:46:50.865
There will be somebody that
will come up to them and say,

00:46:50.865 --> 00:46:52.240
I will give you
a billion dollars

00:46:52.240 --> 00:46:53.853
if you put me on your board.

00:46:53.853 --> 00:46:55.270
And when they
follow the money, it

00:46:55.270 --> 00:46:57.080
was China that
gave him the money,

00:46:57.080 --> 00:46:59.140
gave an American that
money and said, here's

00:46:59.140 --> 00:47:00.847
a billion dollars for free.

00:47:00.847 --> 00:47:02.680
Go and get on the boards
of these companies,

00:47:02.680 --> 00:47:05.500
and your only price
tag is to bring

00:47:05.500 --> 00:47:09.340
me the intellectual property
and the proprietary information.

00:47:09.340 --> 00:47:10.450
And so it's hard.

00:47:10.450 --> 00:47:12.700
A company will come to
me and say, what do I do?

00:47:12.700 --> 00:47:15.370
And I'll say, do
not take the money,

00:47:15.370 --> 00:47:17.440
because you will sell your soul.

00:47:17.440 --> 00:47:20.110
This is where the
government needs to help.

00:47:20.110 --> 00:47:22.120
The government
needs to help make

00:47:22.120 --> 00:47:25.000
sure there is an even
playing field economically,

00:47:25.000 --> 00:47:27.730
or all these fragile
new space companies

00:47:27.730 --> 00:47:30.520
will never build an
industrial base equivalent

00:47:30.520 --> 00:47:33.610
to the aerospace industry or
the shipbuilding industry that

00:47:33.610 --> 00:47:35.950
have made our nation
free and strong

00:47:35.950 --> 00:47:37.750
for the last hundred years.

00:47:37.750 --> 00:47:39.070
And it will die in the crib.

00:47:39.070 --> 00:47:40.900
The Space Force
and everything we

00:47:40.900 --> 00:47:44.470
need to do to protect this
economy will die in the crib,

00:47:44.470 --> 00:47:48.010
and China will own the
information, the gateways,

00:47:48.010 --> 00:47:50.588
the technologies that flood
all the other countries

00:47:50.588 --> 00:47:51.130
of the world.

00:47:51.130 --> 00:47:53.440
Even our friends like
Germany and England

00:47:53.440 --> 00:47:56.200
have 5G, and are getting
more and more of it.

00:47:56.200 --> 00:48:00.500
Our nuclear power plants
have 5G technology in them.

00:48:00.500 --> 00:48:04.520
And those are all riddled
with back doors and spyware

00:48:04.520 --> 00:48:07.840
that can see everything
we're doing as a nation.

00:48:07.840 --> 00:48:09.050
We know it.

00:48:09.050 --> 00:48:11.920
This is like a slow growing
vine around the spinal cord

00:48:11.920 --> 00:48:14.440
of America,
insidiously and slowly,

00:48:14.440 --> 00:48:17.670
because that is the mindset
of the Chinese strategy.

00:48:17.670 --> 00:48:19.010
It is not to fight.

00:48:19.010 --> 00:48:20.240
They don't want to fight.

00:48:20.240 --> 00:48:24.100
They want to dominate the
economic prowess of America

00:48:24.100 --> 00:48:26.710
over 100 years, and we
go out with a whimper.

00:48:30.049 --> 00:48:31.310
MICHAEL ANTON: Over here.

00:48:31.310 --> 00:48:31.810
Sure.

00:48:37.390 --> 00:48:39.840
AUDIENCE: So you
mention the fact

00:48:39.840 --> 00:48:42.950
that the Executive
and the Congress

00:48:42.950 --> 00:48:46.440
affect the military
to the same respect.

00:48:46.440 --> 00:48:49.290
Do you think changing the
public's mind will be helpful

00:48:49.290 --> 00:48:49.862
as well?

00:48:49.862 --> 00:48:51.820
STEVEN QUAST: That's a
great question, and yes.

00:48:51.820 --> 00:48:54.810
There are two groups
of people that do not

00:48:54.810 --> 00:48:57.000
understand what's going on--

00:48:57.000 --> 00:48:58.710
the American people
and Congress.

00:48:58.710 --> 00:49:01.460
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

00:49:02.600 --> 00:49:05.160
STEVEN QUAST: And again, you
know I retired in September.

00:49:05.160 --> 00:49:08.310
And I have been spending
my every waking hour

00:49:08.310 --> 00:49:11.040
helping Congress understand
what's going on here.

00:49:11.040 --> 00:49:15.540
Because it's essentially the
same as China ignoring the Navy

00:49:15.540 --> 00:49:18.720
and regretting it
600 years later when

00:49:18.720 --> 00:49:22.230
their civilization rotted
from within because

00:49:22.230 --> 00:49:25.320
of external players that
stole away their values.

00:49:25.320 --> 00:49:28.800
Or England, that lost an
entire generation of men

00:49:28.800 --> 00:49:32.120
before they realized what the
competition was really about.

00:49:32.120 --> 00:49:35.160
It wasn't about Napoleonic
soldiers shoulder

00:49:35.160 --> 00:49:38.200
to shoulder on a parade
field with courage.

00:49:38.200 --> 00:49:41.730
It was about the
machine gun and gas.

00:49:41.730 --> 00:49:43.380
And it killed them all.

00:49:43.380 --> 00:49:44.870
Deep regret.

00:49:44.870 --> 00:49:47.070
But they went into
it enthusiastic.

00:49:47.070 --> 00:49:50.710
Read the literature
of the time, 1914.

00:49:50.710 --> 00:49:52.845
They couldn't wait to go die.

00:49:52.845 --> 00:49:54.720
They just didn't know
they were going to die.

00:49:54.720 --> 00:49:56.280
They thought courage
would save them.

00:49:56.280 --> 00:49:59.188
They underestimated the
power of technology.

00:49:59.188 --> 00:50:00.480
We're doing the same right now.

00:50:00.480 --> 00:50:03.330
But the enemy is
not as aggressive.

00:50:03.330 --> 00:50:05.010
China is passive.

00:50:05.010 --> 00:50:06.450
China is silent.

00:50:06.450 --> 00:50:08.070
China is insidious.

00:50:08.070 --> 00:50:11.130
China has a 100 year plan.

00:50:11.130 --> 00:50:14.970
One step at a time, a slow
growing vine that slowly

00:50:14.970 --> 00:50:17.950
paralyzes the competition.

00:50:17.950 --> 00:50:19.560
So the American
people need to know.

00:50:19.560 --> 00:50:20.860
They do not know.

00:50:20.860 --> 00:50:22.410
Help me get it to them.

00:50:22.410 --> 00:50:25.260
Congress doesn't fully
know, and the reason

00:50:25.260 --> 00:50:27.780
I know that is not only because
I've been talking to them,

00:50:27.780 --> 00:50:30.100
some do, but they're still
asking this question.

00:50:30.100 --> 00:50:31.560
Why do we need a Space Force?

00:50:31.560 --> 00:50:32.910
It's a waste of money.

00:50:32.910 --> 00:50:34.740
We've got NASA.

00:50:34.740 --> 00:50:36.960
That would be like sending
the wagon trains out west

00:50:36.960 --> 00:50:37.627
with no cavalry.

00:50:45.115 --> 00:50:48.063
MICHAEL ANTON: OK.

00:50:48.063 --> 00:50:49.480
STEVEN QUAST: See
I said something

00:50:49.480 --> 00:50:51.543
that inspired you
to ask a question,

00:50:51.543 --> 00:50:52.460
because you popped up.

00:50:52.460 --> 00:50:53.950
AUDIENCE: Yeah.

00:50:53.950 --> 00:50:55.700
Thanks for coming.

00:50:55.700 --> 00:51:01.100
I want to talk about the balance
of power in the Asia-Pacific.

00:51:01.100 --> 00:51:03.940
I think Japan's
sure to go nuclear.

00:51:03.940 --> 00:51:08.725
They won't maybe in 5
years, maybe 10 years.

00:51:12.250 --> 00:51:17.170
That's going to offset
the Chinese advancing.

00:51:17.170 --> 00:51:18.185
That's what I think.

00:51:18.185 --> 00:51:20.110
STEVEN QUAST: OK, well
let me talk to that,

00:51:20.110 --> 00:51:23.650
because I disagree
fundamentally with that premise.

00:51:23.650 --> 00:51:27.010
And it's not that that wouldn't
necessarily have a short term

00:51:27.010 --> 00:51:29.200
benefit of deterrence.

00:51:29.200 --> 00:51:33.060
But the power of space does
something really important

00:51:33.060 --> 00:51:33.560
here.

00:51:33.560 --> 00:51:35.860
And this is really
where I'm going to end.

00:51:35.860 --> 00:51:37.720
But I'll just do a
little slice of this,

00:51:37.720 --> 00:51:39.760
and then I'll end
with the later part.

00:51:39.760 --> 00:51:41.980
And that is a vision.

00:51:41.980 --> 00:51:44.980
The power of space can
do what Reagan was doing,

00:51:44.980 --> 00:51:47.890
and the physics just
didn't quite close.

00:51:47.890 --> 00:51:49.360
Brilliant Pebbles
was the program

00:51:49.360 --> 00:51:53.230
to put a space base layer
that could see and kill

00:51:53.230 --> 00:51:56.530
any missile launched
the moment we knew

00:51:56.530 --> 00:51:58.990
was launched in a
direction that was

00:51:58.990 --> 00:52:01.300
nefarious to American values.

00:52:01.300 --> 00:52:03.520
And it could be shot
down before it even

00:52:03.520 --> 00:52:05.740
left the geographic
boundaries of whichever

00:52:05.740 --> 00:52:08.680
place it was launched.

00:52:08.680 --> 00:52:11.980
You can build that off a
shelf today, and we have not,

00:52:11.980 --> 00:52:13.420
and China is.

00:52:13.420 --> 00:52:16.390
So Japan going nuclear, no.

00:52:16.390 --> 00:52:19.420
What we could do if we
as an American society

00:52:19.420 --> 00:52:22.930
decided to invest in the
infrastructure of space

00:52:22.930 --> 00:52:25.000
for information
for all Americans.

00:52:25.000 --> 00:52:26.170
Reliable energy.

00:52:26.170 --> 00:52:27.730
Information is
protected, by the way,

00:52:27.730 --> 00:52:29.140
because it's not the internet.

00:52:29.140 --> 00:52:32.910
You can build gateways that
design trust into it, where

00:52:32.910 --> 00:52:35.980
every American can have
their data without having

00:52:35.980 --> 00:52:39.010
to sacrifice their
civil liberties.

00:52:39.010 --> 00:52:42.280
Energy that can be provided
to anybody on planet Earth

00:52:42.280 --> 00:52:43.720
without strings
attached like they

00:52:43.720 --> 00:52:46.840
do with the Uyghurs and
Hong Kong and any individual

00:52:46.840 --> 00:52:49.738
where they hold their parents
hostage if they don't behave

00:52:49.738 --> 00:52:52.030
properly, or they don't get
to go to the right schools,

00:52:52.030 --> 00:52:55.650
or they don't get to buy
the food that's good.

00:52:55.650 --> 00:52:59.610
Space can make ICBMs,
intercontinental ballistic

00:52:59.610 --> 00:53:04.830
missiles, literally
antiques of past wars.

00:53:07.440 --> 00:53:10.110
And then I'll end
with the other vision.

00:53:10.110 --> 00:53:12.720
But that's one vision.

00:53:12.720 --> 00:53:15.312
You can't get rid
of nuclear weapons,

00:53:15.312 --> 00:53:16.770
because you can
always deliver them

00:53:16.770 --> 00:53:19.210
in a backpack or
some other means.

00:53:19.210 --> 00:53:21.690
But you can deliver
the capability

00:53:21.690 --> 00:53:26.160
to dominate marketplaces
economically.

00:53:26.160 --> 00:53:29.880
And you can literally
design a new world order

00:53:29.880 --> 00:53:32.040
that does not have so
much violence built

00:53:32.040 --> 00:53:34.500
into our deterrence model.

00:53:34.500 --> 00:53:38.080
Where if a civilization
is threatening our values,

00:53:38.080 --> 00:53:41.790
we can deter them without
violence in ways they cannot

00:53:41.790 --> 00:53:43.960
compete with.

00:53:43.960 --> 00:53:47.040
So I'd rather not go the
route of arming more people

00:53:47.040 --> 00:53:48.430
with more nuclear weapons.

00:53:48.430 --> 00:53:50.250
We don't have to go
down that paradigm.

00:53:50.250 --> 00:53:53.640
That's getting trapped in
the paradigm of the past.

00:53:53.640 --> 00:53:57.870
I want to move to a new paradigm
where China can't follow,

00:53:57.870 --> 00:54:00.540
and most other countries on
planet Earth cannot follow

00:54:00.540 --> 00:54:02.993
either, but all of our
friends will go with us.

00:54:02.993 --> 00:54:04.410
And the Japanese
are part of that.

00:54:09.282 --> 00:54:11.240
There's a very inquisitive
question right here,

00:54:11.240 --> 00:54:12.790
and that I'm dying to hear.

00:54:12.790 --> 00:54:14.120
AUDIENCE: We'll get to him.

00:54:14.120 --> 00:54:15.078
STEVEN QUAST: Go ahead.

00:54:15.078 --> 00:54:17.980
AUDIENCE: Have we an idea of
the cost of this initiative?

00:54:17.980 --> 00:54:19.555
STEVEN QUAST: Yeah, so the
cost of the initiative--

00:54:19.555 --> 00:54:20.510
AUDIENCE: I'm sure it
will be in phases, but--

00:54:20.510 --> 00:54:21.343
STEVEN QUAST: Right.

00:54:21.343 --> 00:54:24.020
So cost is always the first
question, and bureaucracy.

00:54:24.020 --> 00:54:25.760
Because right now,
what has happened

00:54:25.760 --> 00:54:28.550
is our country has turned
to our military and said,

00:54:28.550 --> 00:54:30.080
build a Space Force.

00:54:30.080 --> 00:54:33.260
And I guarantee you, it'll be
bureaucratic, it'll be big,

00:54:33.260 --> 00:54:36.497
it'll be expensive, and
it won't get the job done.

00:54:36.497 --> 00:54:38.830
That's the nature of the
bureaucracy and the government.

00:54:38.830 --> 00:54:41.970
Now, it will maybe
succeed in 50 years.

00:54:41.970 --> 00:54:44.780
But we don't have that
luxury, because our pacing has

00:54:44.780 --> 00:54:49.250
to be predicated on our
competition, not on the fact

00:54:49.250 --> 00:54:51.522
that we have been unilaterally
dominant economically

00:54:51.522 --> 00:54:53.480
for the last 70 years,
and we could do anything

00:54:53.480 --> 00:54:55.790
at any pace we wanted and
we didn't have to care

00:54:55.790 --> 00:54:57.680
because nobody was competing.

00:54:57.680 --> 00:55:00.140
So here we are sitting on the
shores of Miami Beach with

00:55:00.140 --> 00:55:02.630
our piña colada.

00:55:02.630 --> 00:55:04.670
And we are like,
oh, Space Force.

00:55:04.670 --> 00:55:08.690
Eh, eh, how much is
it going to cost?

00:55:08.690 --> 00:55:10.490
I will tell you.

00:55:10.490 --> 00:55:13.100
You don't build
the Space Force out

00:55:13.100 --> 00:55:16.700
of the coffers of
the taxpayers' money.

00:55:16.700 --> 00:55:19.880
We built an automobile
industry because it

00:55:19.880 --> 00:55:23.210
was so useful to people,
the marketplace built it.

00:55:23.210 --> 00:55:26.330
The computer industry,
the aerospace industry.

00:55:26.330 --> 00:55:29.810
Space is going to be so
useful to all humanity.

00:55:29.810 --> 00:55:32.390
Trillion dollar markets in
telecommunication, trillion

00:55:32.390 --> 00:55:34.370
dollar markets in
transportation.

00:55:34.370 --> 00:55:36.403
Speed is life, speed is money.

00:55:36.403 --> 00:55:37.820
How many people
are willing to get

00:55:37.820 --> 00:55:44.080
from here to Singapore in 39
minutes instead of 39 hours?

00:55:44.080 --> 00:55:45.750
No, not quite that far.

00:55:45.750 --> 00:55:49.700
So I am here to tell you
that, if this is done right,

00:55:49.700 --> 00:55:51.620
the strategy is
to build the space

00:55:51.620 --> 00:55:54.920
force with the profits of the
marketplaces that you dominate.

00:55:54.920 --> 00:55:57.020
And you've got partners
in civil society.

00:55:57.020 --> 00:55:59.270
Elon Musk, Jeff Bezos.

00:55:59.270 --> 00:56:02.270
Elon Musk is going to dominate
transportation and information

00:56:02.270 --> 00:56:06.140
with his starship and his
13,000 satellites for Wi-Fi

00:56:06.140 --> 00:56:06.853
from space.

00:56:06.853 --> 00:56:08.270
We already have
companies that are

00:56:08.270 --> 00:56:10.940
going to have texting
from space next year.

00:56:10.940 --> 00:56:14.860
In fact, their test
satellite is already up.

00:56:14.860 --> 00:56:17.600
And I don't need a
cell tower to text.

00:56:17.600 --> 00:56:21.290
So this is the trick
of free markets.

00:56:21.290 --> 00:56:23.420
You build it with the
profits of the marketplace

00:56:23.420 --> 00:56:24.378
if you design it right.

00:56:24.378 --> 00:56:28.490
That's why all national security
is foundationally economic.

00:56:28.490 --> 00:56:30.480
Hopefully private industry.

00:56:30.480 --> 00:56:32.660
Absolutely, those are
the titans of innovation.

00:56:32.660 --> 00:56:35.360
They aren't bogged down by
a culture of risk aversion

00:56:35.360 --> 00:56:39.320
that bakes into our
government and our military.

00:56:39.320 --> 00:56:41.660
And they're willing
to take risk.

00:56:41.660 --> 00:56:44.030
And those are the only ways
of competing and winning

00:56:44.030 --> 00:56:45.230
in a real race.

00:56:45.230 --> 00:56:48.678
Risk and the
willingness to fail.

00:56:48.678 --> 00:56:49.720
MICHAEL ANTON: All right.

00:56:49.720 --> 00:56:51.110
This will be the last
one, I'll let you--

00:56:51.110 --> 00:56:53.152
STEVEN QUAST: I'd like
this young lady right here

00:56:53.152 --> 00:56:55.900
to say a word.

00:56:55.900 --> 00:56:56.580
Well, I do too.

00:56:56.580 --> 00:56:59.688
[LAUGHS] Here, there's a mic.

00:56:59.688 --> 00:57:01.230
And if it's not a
good question, I'll

00:57:01.230 --> 00:57:02.772
answer the question
I want to answer.

00:57:02.772 --> 00:57:05.860
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

00:57:05.860 --> 00:57:08.410
AUDIENCE: My question
is, what can we

00:57:08.410 --> 00:57:14.380
do to spread this information?

00:57:14.380 --> 00:57:20.030
Because I have--
this is not new.

00:57:20.030 --> 00:57:23.980
We get tidbits of this
through the news media.

00:57:23.980 --> 00:57:29.650
But nothing to the extent that
you have explained it tonight.

00:57:29.650 --> 00:57:35.410
This is critical to the
future of our country.

00:57:35.410 --> 00:57:36.616
This is it.

00:57:36.616 --> 00:57:39.760
STEVEN QUAST: This is where
an educated electorate

00:57:39.760 --> 00:57:44.140
is so key to our Constitution
that our Founding Fathers wrote

00:57:44.140 --> 00:57:45.400
about.

00:57:45.400 --> 00:57:49.580
And do not underestimate
the power of the network.

00:57:49.580 --> 00:57:51.790
One node touching
three other nodes

00:57:51.790 --> 00:57:53.410
that touched three other nodes.

00:57:53.410 --> 00:58:00.880
Is the sage old story of a young
man who really did something

00:58:00.880 --> 00:58:03.530
brilliant for the king,
and the king said, well,

00:58:03.530 --> 00:58:06.730
I don't have a lot of money,
but what can I do to repay you?

00:58:06.730 --> 00:58:08.500
And the man said,
just give me one grain

00:58:08.500 --> 00:58:12.320
of rice on this chessboard
on this first square.

00:58:12.320 --> 00:58:16.030
And on the second
square give me two.

00:58:16.030 --> 00:58:19.330
And keep doubling it for
every piece of the chessboard.

00:58:19.330 --> 00:58:22.000
Now, many of you
probably know this story.

00:58:22.000 --> 00:58:25.180
By the time you have gotten
to the end of the chessboard

00:58:25.180 --> 00:58:28.454
squares, how much
rice do you have?

00:58:28.454 --> 00:58:30.940
AUDIENCE: A lot.

00:58:30.940 --> 00:58:36.770
STEVEN QUAST: OK, so the entire
planet Earth, six feet high.

00:58:36.770 --> 00:58:38.750
That's the power of the network.

00:58:38.750 --> 00:58:41.870
And it's interesting
that we end on a network.

00:58:41.870 --> 00:58:44.400
Because there's another
important point about space.

00:58:44.400 --> 00:58:46.220
So to answer your
question specifically,

00:58:46.220 --> 00:58:48.560
is tell your friends.

00:58:48.560 --> 00:58:49.610
And start reading.

00:58:49.610 --> 00:58:50.782
It is out there.

00:58:50.782 --> 00:58:51.740
It's just hard to find.

00:58:51.740 --> 00:58:55.910
And it's out there, but
just recently in this way,

00:58:55.910 --> 00:59:00.980
because I couldn't write
about this in the Air Force.

00:59:00.980 --> 00:59:04.080
People do not want to
scare the American people.

00:59:04.080 --> 00:59:06.600
And I don't want to
scare them either.

00:59:06.600 --> 00:59:09.650
But for God's sakes, our
future is at stake here.

00:59:09.650 --> 00:59:13.180
We are victims to a strategy
we don't even recognize.

00:59:13.180 --> 00:59:15.680
And as a person who grew up in
a different cultural paradigm

00:59:15.680 --> 00:59:19.610
that can see this clearly, and
has studied this for 33 years,

00:59:19.610 --> 00:59:22.460
I am here to tell
you, it is imminent.

00:59:22.460 --> 00:59:27.260
And the more we can be in the
dark, the happier China is.

00:59:27.260 --> 00:59:29.810
Because then the coup
de grace is done,

00:59:29.810 --> 00:59:32.090
and it is fait accompli.

00:59:32.090 --> 00:59:34.110
And there's nothing
we can do about it.

00:59:34.110 --> 00:59:39.690
And now I believe that America
is so energetic intellectually

00:59:39.690 --> 00:59:41.640
and so courageous
that eventually we

00:59:41.640 --> 00:59:43.050
will fight our way back.

00:59:43.050 --> 00:59:44.940
But the English haven't
even fought their way

00:59:44.940 --> 00:59:52.530
back from World War I. So
the next hundred years,

00:59:52.530 --> 00:59:54.870
the values that will rule
the next hundred years

00:59:54.870 --> 01:00:00.470
will be defined by this next 10
years and who dominates space.

01:00:00.470 --> 01:00:01.850
So here is the vision, though.

01:00:01.850 --> 01:00:06.350
This is why I started by saying,
this is such a happy story.

01:00:06.350 --> 01:00:09.120
You might think, oh my God,
you know, doom and gloom.

01:00:09.120 --> 01:00:11.650
No.

01:00:11.650 --> 01:00:14.210
Here is a story.

01:00:14.210 --> 01:00:16.910
Every technology, even though
people can use technology

01:00:16.910 --> 01:00:20.610
for evil, every technology has
uplifted the human condition

01:00:20.610 --> 01:00:21.110
over time.

01:00:23.750 --> 01:00:27.600
If you take a look
at the human race,

01:00:27.600 --> 01:00:30.510
there are a higher
percentage of human beings

01:00:30.510 --> 01:00:34.800
that have energy, water,
security, food, than ever

01:00:34.800 --> 01:00:36.870
before on planet Earth, ever.

01:00:36.870 --> 01:00:39.900
Now, there's more people, so
there's more people in poverty

01:00:39.900 --> 01:00:41.040
than ever before.

01:00:41.040 --> 01:00:45.170
But the ratio is moving
in a good direction.

01:00:45.170 --> 01:00:47.732
It's because there are more
people that love their children

01:00:47.732 --> 01:00:49.190
and respect other
people than there

01:00:49.190 --> 01:00:52.070
are evil people like
Stalin and Lenin

01:00:52.070 --> 01:00:56.600
and Mao, who would
kill them for power.

01:00:56.600 --> 01:00:59.630
And this Constitution,
I believe,

01:00:59.630 --> 01:01:04.700
is such a unique and
ordained document

01:01:04.700 --> 01:01:07.790
that if we fumble the ball now,
because we don't pay attention

01:01:07.790 --> 01:01:09.800
to technology, and
how it can change

01:01:09.800 --> 01:01:13.090
world power, shame on us.

01:01:13.090 --> 01:01:14.320
But here's the vision.

01:01:14.320 --> 01:01:17.042
The vision is with
a new paradigm

01:01:17.042 --> 01:01:19.500
that space could bring us, if
we built this infrastructure,

01:01:19.500 --> 01:01:21.360
if we had the vision
to build the Panama

01:01:21.360 --> 01:01:25.230
Canal of our age, the
infrastructure of space,

01:01:25.230 --> 01:01:29.040
we can bring clean
and abundant energy

01:01:29.040 --> 01:01:30.900
affordable to every
person on planet Earth

01:01:30.900 --> 01:01:33.750
with no power lines, no
power plants required.

01:01:33.750 --> 01:01:36.330
Central Africa, where I grew up.

01:01:36.330 --> 01:01:39.480
That tribe could have
information and energy

01:01:39.480 --> 01:01:40.920
right now.

01:01:40.920 --> 01:01:43.440
We have machines that can
bring water out of the air

01:01:43.440 --> 01:01:45.923
without energy from space,
where you could just give them

01:01:45.923 --> 01:01:47.340
a piece of technology
and they can

01:01:47.340 --> 01:01:49.920
have clean water with
no pipes, no aquifers,

01:01:49.920 --> 01:01:51.870
no rivers required.

01:01:51.870 --> 01:01:54.000
You can bring
trusted information

01:01:54.000 --> 01:01:56.340
to any person on planet
Earth where they do not

01:01:56.340 --> 01:01:58.650
have to live with a
scourge of an internet that

01:01:58.650 --> 01:02:03.750
was designed to be open
and free, no security.

01:02:03.750 --> 01:02:06.740
Yet we are trapped in that
paradigm, spending ourselves

01:02:06.740 --> 01:02:09.980
into oblivion, into bankruptcy,
trying to make something secure

01:02:09.980 --> 01:02:12.590
that was never
designed to be secure.

01:02:12.590 --> 01:02:15.610
We could bring
secure, trusted data

01:02:15.610 --> 01:02:17.410
to every human being
on planet Earth,

01:02:17.410 --> 01:02:20.890
underpinned by American values
and the American Constitution.

01:02:20.890 --> 01:02:24.730
We could bring medical healing
because of research facilities

01:02:24.730 --> 01:02:30.100
in space that benefit from
zero gravity and a vacuum

01:02:30.100 --> 01:02:33.070
that we can never do in
the terrestrial realm

01:02:33.070 --> 01:02:35.440
without great cost and energy.

01:02:35.440 --> 01:02:39.250
The server farms in America
that are growing exponentially,

01:02:39.250 --> 01:02:42.400
that are sucking
energy beyond belief,

01:02:42.400 --> 01:02:45.280
could be put into space
and no energy required

01:02:45.280 --> 01:02:48.370
because it's freezing up there.

01:02:48.370 --> 01:02:51.890
And the ability to
communicate and compute.

01:02:51.890 --> 01:02:54.980
The faster we can move
to independent operations

01:02:54.980 --> 01:02:58.700
in space, the more secure we
will be, the more differential

01:02:58.700 --> 01:03:02.390
power we'll have as an
economy and as a civilization

01:03:02.390 --> 01:03:06.860
to defend against terrorism and
the despots of Communism that

01:03:06.860 --> 01:03:08.960
are rearing their
ugly head and trying

01:03:08.960 --> 01:03:10.820
to come after
Western civilization

01:03:10.820 --> 01:03:13.400
and attacking the two
foundational weaknesses

01:03:13.400 --> 01:03:16.070
we have built our
entire prosperity on--

01:03:16.070 --> 01:03:17.360
energy and information.

01:03:17.360 --> 01:03:19.940
And both of them are at
risk, and both of them

01:03:19.940 --> 01:03:22.070
are unaffordable to fix.

01:03:22.070 --> 01:03:23.080
So don't struggle.

01:03:23.080 --> 01:03:26.960
We're struggling to get a
secure grid, a resilient grid.

01:03:26.960 --> 01:03:30.920
We're struggling to get secure
data and resilient data.

01:03:30.920 --> 01:03:32.120
Stop struggling.

01:03:32.120 --> 01:03:34.310
Let our inventors
and our innovators

01:03:34.310 --> 01:03:37.400
design a new paradigm to
uplift the human condition

01:03:37.400 --> 01:03:39.170
and have America underwrite it.

01:03:39.170 --> 01:03:41.830
And America will be
the beneficiaries

01:03:41.830 --> 01:03:45.080
to the amount of trillions
of dollars of profit

01:03:45.080 --> 01:03:47.090
to perpetuate those
business cases

01:03:47.090 --> 01:03:49.580
to deliver every human
being on planet Earth

01:03:49.580 --> 01:03:54.260
prosperity and the blessing
that we respect them no matter

01:03:54.260 --> 01:03:57.260
who they are, no matter
what they believe,

01:03:57.260 --> 01:03:59.870
as long as they respect us.

01:03:59.870 --> 01:04:02.930
That's the vision,
that's the joy.

01:04:02.930 --> 01:04:04.130
Not the negative stuff.

01:04:04.130 --> 01:04:08.420
The negative stuff is only if
good men and women do nothing.

01:04:08.420 --> 01:04:10.940
Then the negative
stuff happens and we

01:04:10.940 --> 01:04:13.250
return to our
academicians and say,

01:04:13.250 --> 01:04:15.240
like they did to Dr.
Fisher in England,

01:04:15.240 --> 01:04:18.980
why did we lose a
generation of men?

01:04:18.980 --> 01:04:21.380
A lack of vision,
a lack of strategy.

01:04:21.380 --> 01:04:24.230
Not equipment, their
equipment was brilliant.

01:04:24.230 --> 01:04:26.690
But it wasn't a
machine gun or gas.

01:04:26.690 --> 01:04:28.520
And they didn't
even think about it.

01:04:28.520 --> 01:04:29.990
We're too courageous for that.

01:04:29.990 --> 01:04:32.810
We'll be just fine, just like we
have been for the last hundred

01:04:32.810 --> 01:04:33.570
years.

01:04:33.570 --> 01:04:34.550
And that's what
you hear today is

01:04:34.550 --> 01:04:36.440
you hear, we don't need
a separate Space Force,

01:04:36.440 --> 01:04:38.648
because we want to integrate
it into the Joint Force,

01:04:38.648 --> 01:04:40.490
in the Army, in the
terrestrial fight.

01:04:40.490 --> 01:04:41.900
That's our purpose.

01:04:41.900 --> 01:04:44.180
Not even thinking
beyond the orbits

01:04:44.180 --> 01:04:46.970
into cislunar space and
the trillion dollar markets

01:04:46.970 --> 01:04:48.740
that will come from that.

01:04:48.740 --> 01:04:51.140
We are at a point
in civilization

01:04:51.140 --> 01:04:53.400
where for the first
time in human history,

01:04:53.400 --> 01:04:56.270
we can reach to the
heavens, a gift God

01:04:56.270 --> 01:05:00.620
has given us, for our resources,
our energy, and our information

01:05:00.620 --> 01:05:03.920
in a way that will never
have to scar the earth again

01:05:03.920 --> 01:05:06.020
for all those things we need.

01:05:06.020 --> 01:05:08.000
We need resources
to feed our families

01:05:08.000 --> 01:05:10.220
and shelter our people.

01:05:10.220 --> 01:05:12.260
We need the ability to
defend those things.

01:05:12.260 --> 01:05:13.790
We need the sense
of belonging that

01:05:13.790 --> 01:05:17.450
comes with loving our
families and our tribes.

01:05:17.450 --> 01:05:22.100
And we need to understand
what's going on around us.

01:05:22.100 --> 01:05:23.990
Those are the only
four things we need.

01:05:23.990 --> 01:05:26.720
Resources, defending
the resources, a sense

01:05:26.720 --> 01:05:30.470
of belonging and understanding.

01:05:30.470 --> 01:05:32.966
Space can give us that.

01:05:32.966 --> 01:05:36.050
But the journey of
1,000 miles to the cost

01:05:36.050 --> 01:05:39.590
and the time, people say
is 100 years too soon.

01:05:39.590 --> 01:05:40.990
It's too expensive.

01:05:40.990 --> 01:05:43.610
A journey of 1,000 miles
starts with the first step.

01:05:43.610 --> 01:05:45.330
And we haven't even
taken the first step.

01:05:45.330 --> 01:05:48.560
And if we don't get a National
Defense Authorization Act,

01:05:48.560 --> 01:05:50.720
we will be giving
our competition that

01:05:50.720 --> 01:05:54.590
